<title>AUSTRIA: Waigel-EMU deficit criteria to be strictly applied.</title>
<headline>Waigel-EMU deficit criteria to be strictly applied.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said in an interview published on Tuesday Germany would do all it could to qualify for European monetary union (EMU) and that the criteria for joining the single currency should be strictly applied.</p>
<p>&quot;We will do everything to fulfil the convergence criteria in time,&quot; he told daily Der Standard. &quot;The European Union treaty is unambiguous. The deficit must not exceed three percent.&quot;</p>
</text>
